The Lord of Kāśī is pleased with men who conduct themselves in this way;
and by the grace of the Lord of Kāśī, reaching Kāśī brings about liberation. // 66
He has properly bathed in all sacred fords; he is consecrated for all sacrifices;
he has given all gifts—by whom Kāśī is frequented. // 167
Thus ends the fortieth chapter, named 'The Exposition of the Duties of the Householder,' in the first half of the Kāśīkhaṇḍa in the eighty-one-thousand-verse Saṃhitā of the glorious Skandapurāṇa. // 40
